WEBVTT

00:00:00.890 --> 00:00:04.700
Diggers: a lane battler where you can never rearrange your hand.

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:07.200
Each turn, play cards that sit together in your hand

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:09.650
onto a site between you and a rival.

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:13.680
Beat what's there to take it, and keep the cards you beat as points.

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:16.320
Two players fight over three sites.

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:19.850
With three or four players, you share one site with each neighbor.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:23.260
My run of 5-6-7 can't beat his three 9s,

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:26.710
so I poach the 4 off his run and slot it in.

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:30.670
The catch: I have to give him a card back from anywhere in my hand.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.830
Now my four-card run beats his three 9s.

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:36.780
I take Garden Park and keep his 9s as points.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.750
Empty your hand to end the season.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:43.450
Score captures and sites that you control, minus your cards left in hand.

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:47.640
Forty-five cards, two to four players, and ten to twenty minutes.

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:52.680
Diggers. Play it in your browser at darrendon.com, or email me for a prototype.
